Subject: [PATCH 1/7] feat(ssd): port the SSD brain workflow onto v0.6.0
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

v0.6.0 moved every desktop concern out of lib.rs into app.rs behind the
`gui` feature, so the local add-ons had to be re-targeted rather than
rebased. Upstream had meanwhile absorbed the source-folders work
(source_mirror.rs, BrainSourcesPanel, dry-run SyncPlan, sortable brain
list) and independently implemented the WAL-checkpoint-on-exit this
setup needs, so only the genuinely local pieces are carried here.

- paths.rs: nv_home() now falls back to a plugged-in SSD, located by its
  NEURO-VAULT-STORAGE\.neurovault\brains.json marker rather than by drive
  letter. Placed in paths (not the desktop layer) so neurovault-server
  and the MCP forwarder resolve the same brains. Env vars are trimmed —
  `set VAR=D:\... &&` captures the trailing space into the value.
- app.rs: nv_eject_ssd_brain triggers the elevated NeuroVault-Eject task,
  stops watchers, checkpoints every WAL and drops the mmap + handles.
- app.rs: closing the main window QUITS instead of hiding (upstream's
  default). A hidden-but-running app holds brain.db and a 256 MiB mmap
  open, so Windows refuses to eject the SSD. This reuses upstream's own
  save-then-quit handshake, so a failed save still reopens the window
  with the retained buffer instead of losing data.
- App.tsx: Eject SSD Brain button, with an index-activity probe that
  warns while ingest is still moving. Quits via quit_after_save, since
  ExitRequested swallows a raw exit(0).
- Restores the launcher, watcher, splash, eject and registration scripts,
  the Claude skills, and the python vault helpers.

Not carried: the 0.5.2 window-rebuild fix is unnecessary here — upstream
prevents the close that destroyed the window, so it can no longer happen.

